Screen-shader regions run at their paint order on Windows too.

The DirectX renderer still ran every region in one go at the overlay
boundary, over the fully composed main scene, where the blade path has
split at each region since b3-user-shader-underlays. A backdrop recorded
under the panels (the Milkdrop backdrop, or a backdrop shader that needs
the region pass) painted over the whole window instead, hiding every
panel, and with All Windows on it took the settings window as well. Now
each region batch runs where it stands and the main target comes back
for whatever draws next.

